=== SURVEY (web source = ElevationProfile.tsx) ===
A presentational filled-area chart of elevation (metres) against distance along a route. Props:
  data: ElevationDataPoint[] { index, distance, elevation, speed? }
  currentIndex?  (ARRAY position used for the cursor reference line — web `data[currentIndex].distance`)
  onClickIndex?  (fires with the tapped sample's `.index` FIELD — web `onClickIndex(data[idx].index)`)
  height = 200 ; distanceUnit = 'km' ; className
Body:
  • elevGain reducer: total ascent/descent over consecutive elevation diffs, each Math.round-ed
    → subtitle `↑ ${gain}m  ↓ ${loss}m`.
  • cursorDistance = data[currentIndex].distance (guarded) → <ReferenceLine x=… cyan dashed>.
  • handleClick → onClickIndex(data[activeTooltipIndex].index).
  • data.length === 0 → <ChartContainer><EmptyState message={t('replay.elevation.noData')}/></> with
    the no-data ariaLabel; else <AreaChart> (areaGradient #10b981 @0.4→0.02, AREA_DEFAULTS.type
    'monotone', strokeWidth 2) + CartesianGrid + XAxis(dataKey distance, fmt(v,1), label=distanceUnit)
    + YAxis(fmt(v,0), label='m') + Tooltip(labelFormatter `${fmt(v,2)} ${unit}`, formatter
    `[${fmt(v,0)} m, t('replay.elevation.label','Elevation')]`) + Area(dataKey elevation) and the
    along-the-route ariaLabel.
  • fmt(v,d) = fmtNumber = safeNumber(v).toLocaleString(locale,{min/maxFractionDigits:d})
    (locale-aware grouping; non-finite → 0 via safeNumber).
Data sources (P1/S8): none — purely presentational (the parent owns the fetch + the display-unit
conversion); its only hook is useTranslation (P1/S10). Shared components: charts/ChartContainer,
feedback/EmptyState. Charts: Recharts AreaChart (the prompt's "Charts: (none)" is an extraction
artifact — the source imports the chart primitives from the `@/components/charts` barrel, not from
'recharts' directly; the AreaChart IS reproduced — covenant #5, no parity shortcuts).
i18n keys extracted: replay.elevation.title / .aria (empty) / .noData / .label, plus the populated
ariaLabel ('…along the route, with total gain and loss in meters'). The web source keys BOTH aria
strings under the single id `replay.elevation.aria` (differing only in fallback); to preserve both
spoken labels for VoiceOver parity the populated variant is keyed as `replay.elevation.ariaPopulated`
(documented in the .strings header — covenant #9).

